#: ../../Flocs_Fractals_and_Forces/FFF_Suspensions.rst:12
msgid "Fluidized Suspensions"
msgstr "Suspensiones fluidizadas"

#: ../../Flocs_Fractals_and_Forces/FFF_Suspensions.rst:15
msgid "Suspension Density"
msgstr "Densidad de suspensión"

#: ../../Flocs_Fractals_and_Forces/FFF_Suspensions.rst:17
msgid ""
"Suspension densities will be of interest both in understanding the physics "
"of floc filters fluidized sand beds. The density of a suspension of "
"particles is equal to the mass of the particles and water divided by the "
"suspension volume. In the case of flocs we can track the concentration of "
"the core particles in the suspension and ignore the diameter of the flocs "
"when calculating the suspension density."
msgstr ""
"Las densidades de suspensión serán de interés tanto para entender la física "
"de los filtros de flócs en los lechos de arena fluidizados. La densidad de "
"una suspensión de partículas es igual a la masa de las partículas y el agua "
"dividida por el volumen de la suspensión. En el caso de los flócs, podemos "
"seguir la concentración de las partículas del núcleo en la suspensión e "
"ignorar el diámetro de los flócs al calcular la densidad de la suspensión."

#: ../../Flocs_Fractals_and_Forces/FFF_Suspensions.rst:19
msgid ""
"\\rho_{suspension}\n"
"= \\frac{M_{H_2O} + M_{particles}}{\\forall_{suspension}}\n"
"\n"
"=\\frac{M_{H_2O} }{\\forall_{suspension}} + C_{particles}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Flocs_Fractals_and_Forces/FFF_Suspensions.rst:27
msgid ""
"The mass of water in a suspension, :math:`M_{H_2O}`, must take into account "
"the fraction of the suspension volume occupied by the particles."
msgstr ""
"La masa de agua en una suspensión, :math:`M_{H_2O}`, debe tener en cuenta la"
" fracción del volumen de suspensión ocupada por las partículas."

#: ../../Flocs_Fractals_and_Forces/FFF_Suspensions.rst:29
msgid ""
"\\frac{M_{H_2O}}{\\forall_{suspension} } =\n"
"\\rho_{H_2O} \\left( 1 - \\frac{C_{particles}}{\\rho_{particles}} \\right)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Flocs_Fractals_and_Forces/FFF_Suspensions.rst:35
msgid ""
"where :math:`\\frac{C_{particles}}{\\rho_{particles}}` is the fraction of "
"the suspension volume occupied by the particles. Substituting Equation "
":eq:`water_mass_in_suspension` into Equation :eq:`density_suspension_1` we "
"obtain the density of the suspension."
msgstr ""

#: ../../Flocs_Fractals_and_Forces/FFF_Suspensions.rst:37
msgid ""
"\\rho_{suspension} =\n"
"\\rho_{H_2O} \\left( 1 - \\frac{C_{particles}}{\\rho_{particles}} \\right) +"
" C_{particles}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Flocs_Fractals_and_Forces/FFF_Suspensions.rst:44
msgid ""
"Equation :eq:`density_suspension_2` can be rewritten in terms of the buoyant"
" density to obtain"
msgstr ""
"La ecuación :eq:`density_suspension_2` puede reescribirse en función de la "
"densidad de flotabilidad para obtener"

#: ../../Flocs_Fractals_and_Forces/FFF_Suspensions.rst:46
msgid ""
"\\rho_{suspension} - \\rho_{H_2O} =\n"
"  C_{particles}\\left(1 - \\frac{\\rho_{H_2O}}{\\rho_{particles}}\\right)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Flocs_Fractals_and_Forces/FFF_Suspensions.rst:54
msgid "Fluidized Bed Porosity"
msgstr "Porosidad del lecho fluidizado"

#: ../../Flocs_Fractals_and_Forces/FFF_Suspensions.rst:56
msgid ""
"AguaClara plants have two fluidized beds. The first is the floc filter that "
"forms in the bottom of the clarifiers and the second is the sand in the "
"filters during backwash. The equations describing fluidized beds require "
"multiple steps in the calculations and are easily handled in Python. The "
"following equations are available in a `Colab worksheet "
"<https://colab.research.google.com/github/AguaClara-"
"Reach/Textbook/blob/master/Flocs_Fractals_and_Forces/Colab/FFF.ipynb>`_ and "
"the equations are from `this paper "
"<https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ijheatmasstransfer.2004.08.008>`_."
msgstr ""
"Las plantas de AguaClara tienen dos camas fluidizadas. La primera es la "
"filtro de flóculos que se forma en la parte inferior de los clarificadores y"
" la segunda es la arena de los filtros durante el retrolavado. Las "
"ecuaciones que describen las camas fluidizadas requieren varios pasos en los"
" cálculos y se manejan fácilmente en Python. Las siguientes ecuaciones están"
" disponibles en una hoja de cálculo `Colab "
"<https://colab.research.google.com/github/AguaClara-"
"Reach/Textbook/blob/master/Flocs_Fractals_and_Forces/Colab/FFF.ipynb>`_ y "
"las ecuaciones son de `este artículo "
"<https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ijheatmasstransfer.2004.08.008>`_."

#: ../../Flocs_Fractals_and_Forces/FFF_Suspensions.rst:58
msgid ""
"The hydraulic diameter is needed to account for wall effects for small "
"reactors."
msgstr ""
"El diámetro hidráulico es necesario para tener en cuenta los efectos de "
"pared en reactores pequeños."

#: ../../Flocs_Fractals_and_Forces/FFF_Suspensions.rst:60
msgid "D_{H}={\\frac {4A}{P}}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Flocs_Fractals_and_Forces/FFF_Suspensions.rst:65
#: ../../Flocs_Fractals_and_Forces/FFF_Suspensions.rst:77
#: ../../Flocs_Fractals_and_Forces/FFF_Suspensions.rst:101
msgid "where"
msgstr "donde"

#: ../../Flocs_Fractals_and_Forces/FFF_Suspensions.rst:66
msgid ":math:`D_{H}` is the hydraulic diameter"
msgstr ":math:`D_{H}` es el diámetro hidráulico"

#: ../../Flocs_Fractals_and_Forces/FFF_Suspensions.rst:67
msgid ":math:`A` is the plan view area"
msgstr ":math:`A` es el área de vista en planta"

#: ../../Flocs_Fractals_and_Forces/FFF_Suspensions.rst:68
msgid ":math:`P` is the wetted perimeter"
msgstr ":math:`P` es el perímetro mojado"

#: ../../Flocs_Fractals_and_Forces/FFF_Suspensions.rst:70
msgid ""
"For reactors with dimensions that are not much larger than the dimensions of"
" the flocs it is necessary to correct for wall effects. This correction will"
" be important for laboratory scale and some pilot scale reactors. The "
"terminal velocity of a particle corrected for wall effects is"
msgstr ""
"Para reactores cuyas dimensiones no son mucho mayores que las de los "
"flóculos, es necesario corregir para efectos de pared. Esta corrección será "
"importante para reactores a escala de laboratorio y algunos a escala piloto."
" La velocidad terminal de una partícula corregida para efectos de pared es"

#: ../../Flocs_Fractals_and_Forces/FFF_Suspensions.rst:72
msgid "v_{t_w} = \\frac{v_t}{10^{\\frac{D_{particle}}{D_H}}}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Flocs_Fractals_and_Forces/FFF_Suspensions.rst:78
msgid ""
":math:`v_t` terminal velocity in an infinite fluid obtained from Equation "
":eq:`v_t_general`"
msgstr ""
":math:`v_t` velocidad terminal en un fluido infinito obtenida de la ecuación"
" :eq:`v_t_general`"

#: ../../Flocs_Fractals_and_Forces/FFF_Suspensions.rst:80
msgid ""
"The Reynolds number :math:`Re_t` is based on the terminal velocity of the "
"particle."
msgstr ""
"El número de Reynolds :math:`Re_t` se basa en la velocidad terminal de la "
"partícula."

#: ../../Flocs_Fractals_and_Forces/FFF_Suspensions.rst:82
msgid "Re_t = \\frac{v_t D_{particle}}{\\nu}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Flocs_Fractals_and_Forces/FFF_Suspensions.rst:87
msgid ""
"The fluidization index, z, is a function of the Reynolds number at the "
"terminal velocity."
msgstr ""
"El índice de fluidización, z, es una función del número de Reynolds en la "
"velocidad terminal."

#: ../../Flocs_Fractals_and_Forces/FFF_Suspensions.rst:89
msgid ""
"z=\\frac{0.65\\left(2+0.5 Re_t^{0.65}\\right)}{\\left(1+0.5 "
"Re_t^{0.65}\\right)}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Flocs_Fractals_and_Forces/FFF_Suspensions.rst:94
msgid "The following equation is used to find the porosity of a fluidized bed."
msgstr ""
"La siguiente ecuación se utiliza para determinar la porosidad de un lecho "
"fluidizado."

#: ../../Flocs_Fractals_and_Forces/FFF_Suspensions.rst:96
msgid ""
"\\phi=\\left(\\frac{\\bar v_z}{v_{t_w}}\\right)^{1 / "
"z}\\left(1-\\phi_{\\mathrm{SB}}\\right)+\\phi_{\\mathrm{SB}}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Flocs_Fractals_and_Forces/FFF_Suspensions.rst:102
msgid ":math:`v_{t_w}` particle terminal velocity corrected for wall effect"
msgstr ":math:`v_{t_w}` velocidad terminal de partícula corregida por efecto muro"

#: ../../Flocs_Fractals_and_Forces/FFF_Suspensions.rst:103
msgid ":math:`\\bar v_z` superficial liquid velocity (our upflow velocity)"
msgstr ""
":math:`\\bar v_z` velocidad superficial del líquido (nuestra velocidad de "
"flujo ascendente)"

#: ../../Flocs_Fractals_and_Forces/FFF_Suspensions.rst:104
msgid ":math:`z` is the fluidization index"
msgstr ":math:`z` es el índice de fluidización"

#: ../../Flocs_Fractals_and_Forces/FFF_Suspensions.rst:105
msgid ""
":math:`\\phi_{\\mathrm{SB}}` is the static bed pore volume fraction which we"
" will assume is 0.4"
msgstr ""

